{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"54acc6cb170f58919433d45618a20bc66e555aa81a951d05be23ae8ee3920d22","packTokens":2033,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":252,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":542,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1132,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"A web front end with a small API and a database behind it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"The app ships with exactly 8 requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests are stored in the database and survive a reload and a restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The API needs these four operations and no others: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests screen with status filters, create dialog, and loading, empty, and error states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Request detail screen with status-appropriate action, update failure state, and not-found state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Clean light theme, responsive layout, accessible controls, and specified badge colors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Automated tests for the business rules and one end-to-end workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"If the user creates a request while a status filter other than All is selected, how should the list behave after successful creation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No specific browser support target beyond browsers compatible with the chosen implementation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, what should the dialog show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, keep the entered values, and allow retry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should surrounding whitespace in a title affect requiredness, length validation, and the stored title?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim surrounding whitespace before validating and storing the title.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"After a successful status change on the detail screen, what should happen to the Requests list when the user returns to it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the selected filter and refresh the list; the request may disappear if it no longer matches the filter.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 1280 px table-layout target be configurable, or remain the fixed target specified for this release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep 1280 px as the fixed table-layout target.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the request detail screen add states for loading a request and for failures other than not-found?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the specified detail behavior: show the request on success and “Request not found.” for an unknown ID; add no other fetch states.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a maintenance request system with a browser-accessible Requests screen, an HTTP API, and a database that stores request records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"On first initialization of an empty database, seed exactly eight requests: four Open, including exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, representing every supported area.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Persist requests across browser reloads and application restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Expose exactly four API operations: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change a request’s status; reject attempts to edit fixed fields or delete requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Return all requests or requests matching one requested status, ordered newest first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"On valid creation, assign a system-generated ID and UTC creation time and set status to Open.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Require a title trimmed to 3–80 characters, one of the supported areas (Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception), one of the supported priorities (Low, Normal, or Urgent), and an optional description of no more than 500 characters; reject invalid values with an error naming the field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Allow only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status transitions; reject other changes, return not found for an unknown ID, and reject a missing or unrecognized status without changing the request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show the Hive Works wordmark, demo-user initials SC, status filters All, Open, In progress, and Done with All initially selected, a New request button, and a newest-first request list on the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Load the list for the selected filter and retain that filter when returning from request detail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show a New request dialog with Title, Area, Priority defaulting to Normal, and Description fields, plus Create and Cancel controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"After successful creation, close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top of the list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"For field validation failures, keep the dialog open and show the error under the affected field; for other create failures, show “Could not create request.”, retain entered values, and allow retry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Show the appropriate loading, empty, or load-error state on the Requests screen, with retry available for load errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show request detail with a back link, title, area, priority and status badges, created date, and description or “No description.” when empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show Start work for Open requests, Mark done for In progress requests, and Reopen for Done requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"After a successful status change, show the new status and corresponding action; after failure, show “Could not update the request.” and retain the prior status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"For an unknown request ID, show “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Use a light theme, one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and labeled status and priority badges with Open blue, In progress amber, Done green, Urgent red, and Low and Normal neutral.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Display dates as date-only values, such as “8 Oct 2026,” without time or timezone; use stacked cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px, with no horizontal page scrolling at those widths.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Label every field, make every control keyboard reachable, and meet WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Include automated tests for the request business rules and an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}